    "q-80539": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80539",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]$ is a non-zero vector that is orthogonal to the set $W=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\},$ find the value of $\\frac{b+c}{a}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=5$, we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=-1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=5.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b+c}{a}=\\frac{-2+5}{-1}=-3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
