    "q-140469": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140469",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find ${H}^{⊥}$ if $H=\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote the vectors that span the subspace $H$ as ${h}_{1}$ and ${h}_{2}.$ \n\nA vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0$ and $x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0 \\\\ x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-14{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -14 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one), so ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{7}{4}{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our orthogonal complement is\n\n$$\n{H}^{⊥}=\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
